DERIVED FROM

This project is a derivative work of:

  GLM-5.3-Flash EXL3 on 2x DGX Spark with TensorFold
  https://github.com/MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold
  Copyright 2026 MiaAI-Lab. Apache License, Version 2.0.

Mia's AI Lab wrote the serving recipe this project is built on: the TensorFold container build, the two-rank
start/stop flow over the ConnectX-7 link, and all 53 files in patches/. That work is theirs, and it is the reason
this recipe exists at all. Their NOTICE is reproduced below in full, as Apache-2.0 section 4 requires.

Changes made in this project, relative to the upstream recipe (Apache-2.0, section 4(b)):

  * Serves cantina-security/apex-flash-1 instead of zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash. The two checkpoints share the
    glm5_next architecture exactly, so patches/ is carried over unmodified from upstream.
  * Added quantize/, a new EXL3 conversion pipeline for the apex-flash-1 BF16 release. It streams the 642.7 GB
    source from Hugging Face shard by shard and evicts consumed shards as the converter advances, so the
    conversion fits on a single Spark's disk instead of needing roughly 1 TB. This code is new and is this
    project's own work.
  * Changed the defaults in scripts/config.sh to leave headroom on each Spark for other GPU work: a 262,144-token
    context instead of 1,048,576, a larger memory reserve, vision off, and the checkpoint's own MTP head as the
    default drafter instead of DFlash2. Upstream's settings remain available as profiles/max-context.sh.
  * Added profiles/, tools/bench.py and the verification steps described in README.md.
  * Fixed the worker disk check in scripts/prepare.sh to count the part of the checkpoint
    the worker already holds. The copy is incremental, but the check asked for room for a
    second full copy, so updating a checkpoint in place was refused on a worker that had
    nearly all of it.

patches/ is unmodified upstream work. scripts/ and start.sh / stop.sh are upstream files with the changes above.


